BALTIMORE — On the outside looking into the NCAA Tournament for 24 years, Northeastern today took a big step toward earning an invitation to the Big Dance.
In a game that featured nine lead changes and five ties, the Huskies took control down the stretch to score a 78-71 victory over UNC Wilmington in a Colonial Athletic Tournament semfinal at Royal Farms Arena.
The Huskies (22-11), who now have won their most games in a season since 1990-1991, advance to their second CAA championship game in three years. Tomorrow at 7, they will face top-seeded William & Mary, a 92-91 winner over Hofstra in double-overtime earlier in the day.
